{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1912 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e7b3f001147df785453e69ee942c10dc0aca8be3e81b0651c2fd54dd33fda462" :edb/db-before-t 1911 :edb/db-after-t 1912 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535224 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:55:15.086Z" 13194139535224 true] [17592186064254 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338518 13194139535224 true] [17592186068631 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338527 13194139535224 true] [17592186092329 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338521 13194139535224 true] [17592186092330 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338524 13194139535224 true] [17592186092333 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338512 13194139535224 true] [17592186096532 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338515 13194139535224 true] [17592186096552 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338530 13194139535224 true] [17592186100869 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338506 13194139535224 true] [17592186100929 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338509 13194139535224 true] [17592186105811 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338503 13194139535224 true] [17592186338503 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338504 13194139535224 true] [17592186338503 1089 "q-167689" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338503 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535224 true] [17592186338503 1100 "Consider the function $f(x),$ defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x, & x\\le 1 \\\\ x+a, & 1<x<3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nIt is known that $f$ is continuous at $x=1.$ Find the value of $a.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $a=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338503 1113 #uuid "fe5f2d43-9b41-5a57-a075-65354d6721c4" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338503 1145 "We're told that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1.$ According to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)$ exists.\n\nIn order for ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)$ to exist, the left- and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal.\n\n* Approaching from the left, we have $x<1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)={e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}({e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x) \\\\  & ={e}^{1}+{1}^{2}+1 \\\\  & =e+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n* Approaching from the right, we have $x>1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=x+a.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(x+a) \\\\  & =1+a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the left and right-sided limits must be equal, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) \\\\ 1+a & =e+2 \\\\ a & =e+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338505 13194139535224 true] [17592186338504 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535224 true] [17592186338504 1041 "field-1" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338504 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338505 13194139535224 true] [17592186338504 1110 #uuid "a83994ea-97d2-5f3f-85cd-bbdebe4d60db" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338505 1034 "e+1" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338505 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535224 true] [17592186338505 1111 #uuid "5f1dbf0e-4825-58b0-a33c-3c172a949d77" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338506 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338507 13194139535224 true] [17592186338506 1089 "q-167691" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338506 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535224 true] [17592186338506 1100 "Consider the function $f(x),$ defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x, & x\\le 1 \\\\ x+a, & 1<x<3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nIt is known that $f$ is continuous at $x=1.$ Find the value of $a.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $a=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $e+1$\n\nCurrent part:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+2}{f(x)}=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338506 1113 #uuid "a06ae8a3-e6d2-5ca0-919e-a29d0ee59dfd" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338506 1145 "In part 1, we found that ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=e+2\\ne 0.$\n\nApplying the quotient rule for limits, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+2}{f(x)} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 1}{x}^{3}+2}{{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{3}+2}{e+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{e+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338507 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338508 13194139535224 true] [17592186338507 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535224 true] [17592186338507 1041 "field-1" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338507 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338508 13194139535224 true] [17592186338507 1110 #uuid "84ed7191-fa05-54cc-8438-8151abad81cc" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338508 1034 "\\frac{3}{e+2}" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338508 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535224 true] [17592186338508 1111 #uuid "e18e3cc4-44e0-5469-98af-4c0bc11ea45c" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338509 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338510 13194139535224 true] [17592186338509 1089 "q-167692" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338509 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535224 true] [17592186338509 1100 "Consider the function $f(x),$ defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x, & x\\le 1 \\\\ x+a, & 1<x<3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nIt is known that $f$ is continuous at $x=1.$ Find the value of $a.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $a=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $e+1$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+2}{f(x)}=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3}{e+2}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nConsider the part of $f(x)$ that's defined on the interval $x\\in [3,c],$ where $c>3.$ Calculate the value of $c$ such that the average rate of change over $[3,c]$ is equal to $6.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $c=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338509 1113 #uuid "8a7342b9-5d95-5d61-95de-165eeb082b9f" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338509 1145 "Over the interval $x\\in [3,c],$ we use the expression $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x.$\n\nLet's calculate the average rate of change of $f(x)$ over the interval $[3,c]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(c)-f(3)}{c-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{({c}^{2}-2c)-({3}^{2}-2\\cdot 3)}{c-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}^{2}-2c-3}{c-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{(c-3)(c+1)}{c-3} \\\\  & =c+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want this average rate of change to be equal to $6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =6 \\\\ c+1 & =6 \\\\ c & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338511 13194139535224 true] [17592186338510 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535224 true] [17592186338510 1041 "field-1" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338510 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338511 13194139535224 true] [17592186338510 1110 #uuid "42069d56-c0d8-5410-851c-23ec50d8c54f" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338511 1034 "5" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338511 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535224 true] [17592186338511 1111 #uuid "41688bf0-946a-5d63-9119-67a3d42b7613" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338512 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338513 13194139535224 true] [17592186338512 1089 "q-167693" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338512 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535224 true] [17592186338512 1100 "Consider the function $f(x),$ defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{a