$ | $15$ |\n| $6$ | $24$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain the following approximation for our area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(8+15+24)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =47\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338528 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338529 13194139535224 true] [17592186338528 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535224 true] [17592186338528 1041 "field-1" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338528 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338529 13194139535224 true] [17592186338528 1110 #uuid "9e6514d6-689c-5bcc-bbd9-6068e36742ff" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338529 1034 "47" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535224 true] [17592186338529 1111 #uuid "822e7603-642b-51af-b9dd-abf7c4dc7847" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338530 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338531 13194139535224 true] [17592186338530 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338533 13194139535224 true] [17592186338530 1089 "q-167699" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338530 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535224 true] [17592186338530 1100 "Consider the function $f(x),$ defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x, & x\\le 1 \\\\ x+a, & 1<x<3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nIt is known that $f$ is continuous at $x=1.$ Find the value of $a.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $a=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $e+1$\n\nEarlier pa