n\nWrite down an expression for the area $A$ as a definite integral, and express the integral as the limit of a left Riemann sum. You do not need to simplify your answers.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A={\\int }_{4}^{7}$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338530 1113 #uuid "fb814d14-bc3a-58f3-a0ee-994c3b65af5e" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338530 1145 "We want to express the area $A$ between $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=4$ and $x=7$ as the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{4}^{7}({x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThis definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n\t\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral above, the function is $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x,$ the lower bound is $a=4,$ and the upper bound is $b=7.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{7-4}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{7}({x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[f(4+k\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[f(4+\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{(4+\\frac{3k}{n})}^{2}-2(4+\\frac{3k}{n})]\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338532 13194139535224 true] [17592186338531 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535224 true] [17592186338531 1041 "field-1" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338531 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338532 13194139535224 true] [17592186338531 1110 #uuid "8debbda0-ab9b-5dec-b3f2-1270377cad1e" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338532 1034 "x^2-2x" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535224 true] [17592186338532 1111 #uuid "b6d26561-ab7a-50c6-858f-33f211fc3cac" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338533 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338534 13194139535224 true] [17592186338533 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535224 true] [17592186338533 1041 "field-2" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338533 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338534 13194139535224 true] [17592186338533 1110 #uuid "7e280c85-d8e8-5dc7-9776-323f864a2a97" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338534 1034 "\\frac{3}{n}\\left(\\left(4+\\frac{3k}{n}\\right)^2-2\\left(4+\\frac{3k}{n}\\right)\\right)" 13194139535224 true] [17592186338534 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535224 true] [17592186338534 1111 #uuid "1876c6b6-2344-5cdf-a287-21020ca49dd4" 13194139535224 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-167689" 17592186338503 "q-167689/field-1" 17592186338504 "q-167689/field-1/5a1fe28b022029f27455dc36a9cc0dbfd0eced118